MODULE 2: Footprinting & Reconnaissance

Ab actual hacking methodology ka next step.

10. Footprinting kya hai?

Footprinting = Target ke baare mein information collect karna.

Attacker ya ethical hacker target ko samajhne ke liye information collect karta hai.

Examples:

Domain
IP address
DNS information
Employees
Email IDs
Network information
Technologies
Subdomains
Main idea:

Target ko attack karne se pehle target ko samjho.

11. Passive vs Active Reconnaissance ⭐
Passive Reconnaissance

Target se direct interaction minimum/avoid karke publicly available information collect karna.

Examples:

Search engines
Social media
Public websites
WHOIS
Public DNS records
Active Reconnaissance

Target ke systems/services ke saath direct interaction karke information collect karna.

Examples:

Ping
DNS queries
Traceroute
Network scanning
Difference:

Passive → target ko directly touch nahi karna
Active → target se directly information/query lena

12. DNS Information

DNS = Domain Name System

Ye domain name ko IP address se associate karta hai.

Example:

example.com → IP address

Reconnaissance mein DNS se useful information mil sakti hai, jaise:

IP addresses
DNS servers
Mail servers
Subdomains
Different DNS records

Sir ke material mein DNS enumeration bhi covered hai.

13. WHOIS

WHOIS ka use domain ke registration-related information ko identify karne ke liye kiya ja sakta hai.

Information mein organization/registrar-related details mil sakti hain, depending on privacy protections.

14. Search Engines & Public Information

Search engines bhi reconnaissance ka important source hain.

Publicly available information se attacker target ke:

Employees
Technologies
Documents
Subdomains
Publicly exposed information

identify kar sakta hai.

15. Attack Surface

Attack surface = system ke woh possible entry points jahan se attacker attack attempt kar sakta hai.

Example:

Website + APIs + open ports + login panels + exposed services.

Simple:

More exposed entry points = larger attack surface
DNS Enumeration — Hinglish

DNS Enumeration ka matlab hai target domain ke DNS records aur related information collect karna, jaise:

A Record → Domain ka IP address
AAAA Record → IPv6 address
MX Record → Mail server
NS Record → Authoritative name servers
CNAME Record → Alias of another domain
TXT Record → Additional text/security information
SOA Record → Domain ki authoritative DNS information

Purpose: Target ke infrastructure, subdomains, mail servers aur DNS configuration ko samajhna.

Common tools: nslookup, dig, host, dnsenum

Example:

nslookup example.com
dig example.com
dig example.com MX
dig example.com NS

Exam point: DNS enumeration = DNS records collect karke target ke network/infrastructure ke baare mein information gathering karna.
